'''Arvid Anand Olof Lindblad''' ({{IPA|sv|ˈǎrːvɪd anɑːnd ˈûːlɔf ˈlɪnːdˌblɑːd|lang}}; born 8 August 2007) is a British and Swedish [[racing driver]] who competes in [[Formula One]] for [[Racing Bulls]] under a British flag.

Born in Westminster, London and raised in [[Virginia Water]] to a Swedish father and a [[British Indian]] mother, Lindblad began competitive [[kart racing]] aged seven, winning several continental titles before graduating to [[junior formulae]] in [[2022 Italian F4 Championship|2022]]. A [[protégé]] of [[2024–25 Formula E World Championship|2024–25 Formula E]] World Champion [[Oliver Rowland]], Lindblad contested [[Italian F4]] until [[2023 Italian F4 Championship|2023]], when he finished third overall with [[Prema Racing|Prema]]. After winning the [[2023 Macau Formula 4 Race|Macau F4 Race]], Lindblad progressed to [[FIA Formula 3]] in {{FIAF3|2024}}, achieving several wins and placing fourth, before winning his maiden title in [[2025 Formula Regional Oceania Championship|Formula Regional Oceania]] with [[M2 Competition|M2]]. He advanced to [[FIA Formula 2]] with [[Campos Racing|Campos]] in {{F2|2025}}, becoming the youngest race-winner in [[Formula Two]] history.

A member of the [[Red Bull Junior Team]] since 2021,{{efn-num|Lindblad joined the [[Red Bull Junior Team]] in 2021 as a [[Red Bull GmbH|Red Bull]]–supported driver before becoming a full member when he made his [[Formula 4]] debut [[2022 Italian F4 Championship|in 2022]].<ref name="SIL2026"/>}} Lindblad debuted in Formula One with [[Racing Bulls]] at the {{F1GP|2026|Australian}} in {{F1|2026}}, aged 18.

== Early life ==
Arvid Anand Olof Lindblad was born on 8 August 2007 in [[Virginia Water|Westminster, London.]] His father, Stefan Lindblad, is Swedish and grew up in a [[working-class]] family in [[Småland]], while his mother, Anita ({{nee}} Ahuja), is [[British Indian]]; his maternal grandparents were born in the [[Punjab Province (British India)|Punjab]] region of India before its [[Partition of India|partition into Pakistan]] in 1947, fleeing to [[Delhi]] and later settling in England as doctors in the 1970s.<ref>Per several sources:
* {{Cite web |url=https://www.autosport.com/fia-f3/news/how-red-bulls-next-british-star-earned-a-fast-track-to-f3/10576860/ |title=How Red Bull's next British star earned a fast-track to F3 |last=Simmons |first=Marcus |date=19 February 2024 |website=[[Autosport]] |publisher=[[Motorsport Network]] |access-date=9 September 2024 |issn=0269-946X |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250609124629/https://www.autosport.com/fia-f3/news/how-red-bulls-next-british-star-earned-a-fast-track-to-f3/10576860/ |archive-date=9 June 2025 |url-status=live}}
* {{Cite news |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/articles/c03dn35rk2ko |title='I have two or three years to make it to F1' |last1=Peddy |first1=Chris |last2=Anderson-Jones |first2=Cameron |date=29 April 2024 |work=[[BBC Sport]] |publisher=[[BBC]] |access-date=7 March 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20251218024229/https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/articles/c03dn35rk2ko |archive-date=18 December 2025 |url-status=live}}
* {{Cite news |url=https://www.telegraph.co.uk/formula-1/2026/02/10/arvid-lindblad-british-f1-rookie-indian-swedish-heritage/ |url-access=registration |title=Arvid Lindblad interview: The British F1 rookie inspired by his Indian and Swedish heritage |last=Cary |first=Tom |date=10 February 2026 |work=[[The Daily Telegraph]] |publisher=[[Telegraph Media Group]] |access-date=7 March 2026 |issn=0307-1235 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260307135124/https://www.telegraph.co.uk/formula-1/2026/02/10/arvid-lindblad-british-f1-rookie-indian-swedish-heritage/ |archive-date=7 March 2026 |url-status=live}}
* {{Cite news |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/formula1/articles/c1kgz78klv9o |title=The 'rare combination' behind Britain's youngest F1 driver |last=Benson |first=Andrew |date=25 February 2026 |work=[[BBC Sport]] |publisher=[[BBC]] |access-date=7 March 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260302173701/https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/formula1/articles/c1kgz78klv9o |archive-date=2 March 2026 |url-status=live}}
* {{Cite web |url=https://www.redbull.com/in-en/arvid-lindblad-indian-connections |title=Arvid Lindblad, the new poster child of Indian motorsports |last=Sequeira |first=Sean |date=15 January 2026 |website=[[Red Bull]] |publisher=[[Red Bull GmbH]] |access-date=7 March 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260307135320/https://www.redbull.com/in-en/arvid-lindblad-indian-connections/ |archive-date=7 March 2026 |url-status=live}}</ref> He has stated that he is "very proud of [his] heritage", which "shaped who [he is]", and that he is additionally "very proud to be British".<ref name="BBC2026">{{Cite news |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/formula1/articles/c1kgz78klv9o |title=The 'rare combination' behind Britain's youngest F1 driver |last=Benson |first=Andrew |date=25 February 2026 |work=[[BBC Sport]] |publisher=[[BBC]] |access-date=7 March 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260302173701/https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/formula1/articles/c1kgz78klv9o |archive-date=2 March 2026 |url-status=live}}</ref><ref name="INDY2026"/> His parents both worked in finance in the [[City of London]] and later started their own businesses.<ref name="TIMES2026">{{Cite news |url=https://www.thetimes.com/sport/formula-one/article/arvid-lindblad-why-brains-of-british-teen-will-help-in-debut-year-s8nxr7h57 |url-access=subscription |title=Arvid Lindblad: Why 'brains' of British teen will help in debut year |last=Hudson |first=Molly |date=28 February 2026 |work=[[The Times]] |publisher=[[News UK]] |access-date=7 March 2026 |issn=0140-0460 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260307135434/https://www.thetimes.com/sport/formula-one/article/arvid-lindblad-why-brains-of-british-teen-will-help-in-debut-year-s8nxr7h57 |archive-date=7 March 2026 |url-status=live}}</ref>

Lindblad was raised in Virginia Water, alongside his younger brother, and educated at the [[Royal Grammar School, Guildford|Royal Grammar School]] in [[Guildford]] until he moved into home-schooling aged 15.<ref name="AS2024">{{Cite web |url=https://www.autosport.com/fia-f3/news/how-red-bulls-next-british-star-earned-a-fast-track-to-f3/10576860/ |title=How Red Bull's next British star earned a fast-track to F3 |last=Simmons |first=Marcus |date=19 February 2024 |website=[[Autosport]] |publisher=[[Motorsport Network]] |access-date=9 September 2024 |issn=0269-946X |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250609124629/https://www.autosport.com/fia-f3/news/how-red-bulls-next-british-star-earned-a-fast-track-to-f3/10576860/ |archive-date=9 June 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref><ref name="BBC2024">{{Cite news |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/articles/c03dn35rk2ko |title='I have two or three years to make it to F1' |last1=Peddy |first1=Chris |last2=Anderson-Jones |first2=Cameron |date=29 April 2024 |work=[[BBC Sport]] |publisher=[[BBC]] |access-date=7 March 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20251218024229/https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/articles/c03dn35rk2ko |archive-date=18 December 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref><ref name="TG2026">{{Cite news |url=https://www.telegraph.co.uk/formula-1/2026/02/10/arvid-lindblad-british-f1-rookie-indian-swedish-heritage/ |url-access=registration |title=Arvid Lindblad interview: The British F1 rookie inspired by his Indian and Swedish heritage |last=Cary |first=Tom |date=10 February 2026 |work=[[The Daily Telegraph]] |publisher=[[Telegraph Media Group]] |access-date=7 March 2026 |issn=0307-1235 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260307135124/https://www.telegraph.co.uk/formula-1/2026/02/10/arvid-lindblad-british-f1-rookie-indian-swedish-heritage/ |archive-date=7 March 2026 |url-status=live}}</ref> He was a straight-A student, completing [[A-level]]s in mathematics and chemistry, telling ''[[The Independent]]'' in 2026 that he prefers [[STEM]] subjects due to his [[dyslexia]] and he "tried to mix both [racing and education], which [helped him] become who [he is] today".<ref name="INDY2026"/> He was diagnosed with [[coeliac disease]] when he was 13, which hindered his growth.<ref name="TG2026"/> His involvement in motorsport began when he was given a [[motocross]] bike aged three, a discipline his father contested at a young age.<ref name="AS2024"/><ref name="BBC2026"/> His weekends spent with grandparents in [[Bolton]] resulted in frequent visits to [[RAF_Hooton_Park#Kart circuit|Hooton Park Circuit]] in [[Birkenhead]].<ref name="INDY2026">{{Cite news |url=https://www.independent.co.uk/f1/arvid-lindblad-interview-f1-2026-season-racing-bulls-b2926969.html |title=Arvid Lindblad: 'I told Lando Norris five years ago I'd be in F1 – it's always been my dream' |last=Jackson |first=Kieran |date=2 March 2026 |work=[[The Independent]] |access-date=7 March 2026 |issn=1741-9743 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260303133957/https://www.independent.co.uk/f1/arvid-lindblad-interview-f1-2026-season-racing-bulls-b2926969.html |archive-date=3 March 2026 |url-status=live}}</ref> He used [[sim racing]] to account for missed track time.<ref name="TIMES2026"/>

== Junior racing career ==
=== Karting (2015–2022) ===
Lindblad first started [[karting]] aged five at [[Daytona Motorsport|Daytona Sandown Park]] in [[Esher]].<ref name="AS2024"/> He progressed to competitive kart racing in 2015.<ref name=":2">{{Cite web |last=Gascoigne |first=Roger |date=2022-12-12 |title=Red Bull junior Lindblad switches to Prema for first full F4 season |url=https://formulascout.com/red-bull-junior-lindblad-switches-to-prema-for-first-full-f4-season/101810 |access-date=2023-11-04 |website=Formula Scout |language=en-US}}</ref> Aged nine, Lindblad was taken under the wing of [[Oliver Rowland]].<ref name="AS2024"/> In 2020 he won the [[WSK Super Master Series]] in the [[OKJ (karting)|OKJ]] class.<ref name=":1">{{Cite web |last=Wood |first=Ida |date=2020-12-26 |title=The top karting stars of 2020 |url=https://formulascout.com/the-top-karting-stars-of-2020/73153 |access-date=2023-11-04 |website=Formula Scout |language=en-US}}</ref> Signing to the [[Red Bull Junior Team]] in 2021,<ref>{{Cite web |title=Another great year ahead for the Red Bull Juniors |url=https://www.redbull.com/int-en/juniorteam/another-great-year-ahead-for-the-red-bull-juniors |access-date=2022-09-22 |website=Red Bull |language=en}}</ref> he won the [[WSK Euro Series]] and the [[WSK Final Cup]] for [[OK (karting)|OK]] karts.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Wood |first=Ida |date=2021-12-26 |title=The top karting stars of 2021 |url=https://formulascout.com/the-top-karting-stars-of-2021/87915 |access-date=2023-11-04 |website=Formula Scout |language=en-US}}</ref><ref name=":3">{{Cite web |last=Wood |first=Ida |date=2021-11-24 |title=Rowland's Red Bull protege Arvid Lindblad goes to shifter karting in 2022 |url=https://formulascout.com/rowlands-red-bull-protege-arvid-lindblad-goes-to-shifter-karting-in-2022/86882 |access-date=2023-11-04 |website=Formula Scout |language=en-US}}</ref> He moved to shifter karting in 2022.<ref name=":3" /> A major accident occurred during the [[Champions of the Future Winter Series]] kart race where he crashed out during qualifying heat due to contact and suffered a broken thumb and extensive tissue damage.<ref name=":0">{{Cite web |last=Brabner |first=George |date=2022-09-06 |title=Who is Red Bull Junior and new F4 rookie Arvid Lindblad? |url=https://f1feederseries.com/2022/09/06/who-is-red-bull-junior-and-new-f4-rookie-arvid-lindblad/ |access-date=2022-09-22 |website=F1 Feeder Series |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Wood |first=Ida |date=2022-02-27 |title=Red Bull protege Arvid Lindblad injured in karting crash |url=https://formulascout.com/red-bull-protege-arvid-lindblad-injured-in-karting-crash/90109 |access-date=2023-11-04 |website=Formula Scout |language=en-US}}</ref>

=== Formula 4 (2022–2023) ===
==== 2022: Junior formulae debut ====
[[File:F4 Italy 2022 Nr. 31 (2).jpg|thumb|left|Lindblad driving in the [[2022 Italian F4 Championship]] at the [[Red Bull Ring]]]]
In 2022, Lindblad made his debut single-seater racing by joining [[Van Amersfoort Racing]] ahead of the fifth round of the [[2022 Italian F4 Championship|Italian F4 Championship]] after testing outside of race weekends throughout the year.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Allen |first=Peter |date=2022-01-14 |title=Red Bull's Arvid Lindblad to debut in F4 with Van Amersfoort Racing |url=https://formulascout.com/red-bulls-arvid-lindblad-to-debut-in-f4-with-van-amersfoort-racing/88623 |access-date=2023-11-04 |website=Formula Scout |language=en-US}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Wood |first=Ida |date=2022-05-20 |title=Red Bull's Arvid Lindblad fastest in first ever F4 test at Vallelunga |url=https://formulascout.com/red-bulls-arvid-lindblad-fastest-in-first-ever-f4-test-at-vallelunga/93923 |access-date=2023-11-04 |website=Formula Scout |language=en-US}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Wood |first=Ida |date=2022-09-06 |title=Chovet returns to FREC, Italian F4 adds race and rookies at Red Bull Ring |url=https://formulascout.com/chovet-returns-to-frec-italian-f4-adds-race-and-rookies-at-red-bull-ring/98304 |access-date=2023-11-04 |website=Formula Scout |language=en-US}}</ref> He was able to amass three points finishes with his best finish being seventh place, putting him 17th in the standings with twelve points.<ref>{{Cite web|last=Gascoigne|first=Roger|date=4 December 2022|title=Red Bull's Lindblad pleased with his F4 start ahead of full season in 2023|url=https://formulascout.com/red-bulls-lindblad-pleased-with-his-f4-start-ahead-of-full-season-in-2023/101208|access-date=17 February 2025|website=Formula Scout|language=en-GB}} </ref>

==== 2023: Maiden victories ====
Ahead of the season, Lindblad joined [[Hitech Grand Prix]] to compete in the [[2023 Formula 4 UAE Championship|Formula 4 UAE Championship]].<ref>{{Cite web |last=Wood |first=Ida |date=2022-12-29 |title=Red Bull's Lindblad leads cluster of new entries for F4 UAE |url=https://formulascout.com/red-bulls-lindblad-leads-cluster-of-new-entries-for-f4-uae/102367 |access-date=2023-11-04 |website=Formula Scout |language=en-US}}</ref> In race 3 of the opening round held at the [[Dubai Autodrome]], Lindblad took his first [[Formula 4]] win as he fended off [[Ferrari Driver Academy]] driver [[Tuukka Taponen]] from pole position.<ref>{{Cite web|last=Alonso Lopez|first=Alejandro|date=14 January 2023|title=Lindblad earns first car racing win in safety car-filled F4 UAE race three|url=https://formulascout.com/lindblad-earns-first-car-racing-win-in-safety-car-filled-f4-uae-race-three/102874|access-date=17 February 2025|website=Formula Scout|language=en-GB}}</ref><ref name=":4" /> However, this proved a false dawn as Lindblad only scored 26 points in the following two rounds, which dropped him out of the hunt.<ref>{{Cite web|title=Wharton and Rinicella fight back, but Ugochukwu extends his lead: 4 takeaways from F4 UAE Round 2|date=31 January 2023|url=https://feederseries.net/2023/01/31/wharton-and-rinicella-fight-back-but-ugochukwu-extends-his-lead-4-takeaways-from-f4-uae-round-2/|access-date=17 February 2025|website=Feeder Series|language=en}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|title=The championship fight is back on as Wharton slashes Ugochukwu's lead: 3 takeaways from F4 UAE Round 3|date=3 February 2023|url=https://feederseries.net/2023/02/03/the-championship-fight-is-back-on-as-wharton-slashes-ugochukwus-lead-3-takeaways-from-f4-uae-round-3/|access-date=17 February 2025|website=Feeder Series|language=en}}</ref> Despite this, Lindblad notched up a podium during the season finale in [[Yas Marina Circuit|Yas Marina]], putting him fifth in the standings.<ref>{{Cite web|title=Wharton wins title in dramatic finale: 4 takeaways from F4 UAE Round 5|date=20 February 2023|url=https://feederseries.net/2023/02/20/wharton-wins-title-in-dramatic-finale-4-takeaways-from-f4-uae-round-5/|access-date=17 February 2025|website=Feeder Series|language=en}}</ref>

[[File:F4 Italy 2023 Mugello Nr. 23 Lindblad (1).jpg|thumb|right|Lindblad driving in the [[2023 Italian F4 Championship]] at [[Mugello Circuit]]]]
For his main campaign in [[2023 Italian F4 Championship|Italian F4]], Lindblad joined [[Prema Racing]].<ref name=":2" /> He got off to a great start, taking his first win during the [[Imola Circuit|Imola opener]] inclusive of two other podiums.<ref>{{Cite web|title=Italian F4 notes from Imola: Lindblad on top after a spectacular weekend|date=4 May 2023|url=https://feederseries.net/2023/05/04/italian-f4-notes-from-imola-lindblad-on-top-after-a-spectacular-weekend/|access-date=17 February 2025|website=Feeder Series|language=en}}</ref> He then proceeded to secure a double win in [[Misano World Circuit Marco Simoncelli|Misano]].<ref>{{Cite web|title=Italian F4 notes from Misano: Can anyone match Arvid Lindblad?|date=25 May 2023|url=https://feederseries.net/2023/05/25/italian-f4-notes-from-misano-can-anyone-match-arvid-lindblad/|access-date=17 February 2025|website=Feeder Series|language=en}}</ref> An impressive feat followed after winning all three races at [[Monza Circuit]] he opened up his championship lead to over 80 points.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Gascoigne |first=Roger |date=2023-06-25 |title=Lindblad completes Monza hat-trick in thrilling Italian F4 slipstreamer |url=https://formulascout.com/lindblad-completes-hat-trick-in-thrilling-monza-italian-f4-slipstreamer/108494 |access-date=2023-11-04 |website=Formula Scout |language=en-US}}</ref> However during the final three rounds, his Prema machinery began to struggle with a lack of pace, leading to Lindblad not even taking a podium finish.<ref>{{Cite web|last=Wood|first=Ida|date=2 October 2023|title=Prema's Italian F4 drivers admit to pace struggle at Mugello|url=https://formulascout.com/premas-italian-f4-drivers-admit-to-pace-struggle-at-mugello/111725|access-date=17 February 2025|website=Formula Scout|language=en-GB}}</ref> This allowed rivals [[Kacper Sztuka]] and teammate [[Ugo Ugochukwu]] to overhaul him in the standings, leading Lindblad to finish third in the standings.<ref>{{Cite web|last=Scout|first=Formula|date=29 December 2023|title=Formula Scout Top 50 Drivers of 2023: 30-21|url=https://formulascout.com/formula-scout-top-50-drivers-of-2023-30-21/114444|access-date=17 February 2025|website=Formula Scout|language=en-GB}}</ref>

In the [[2023 Euro 4 Championship|Euro 4 Championship]], Lindblad had a solid start as he secured pole for the opening [[Mugello Circuit|Mugello round]], where he went on to finish fourth.<ref>{{Cite web|last=Whitfield|first=Steve|date=7 July 2023|title=Sztuka, Lindblad and Wharton share poles in first ever Euro 4 qualifying|url=https://formulascout.com/sztuka-lindblad-and-wharton-share-poles-in-first-ever-euro-4-qualifying/108904|access-date=17 February 2025|website=Formula Scout|language=en-GB}}</ref> He then went on to take his only Euro 4 win during the final race in [[Monza Circuit|Monza]], and another podium in [[Circuit de Barcelona-Catalunya|Barcelona]] lifted him to fourth in the overall standings.<ref>{{Cite web|last=Wood|first=Ida|date=17 September 2023|title=Lindblad wins Euro 4's third Monza race but is under investigation|url=https://formulascout.com/lindblad-wins-euro-4s-third-monza-race-under-investigation/111431|access-date=17 February 2025|website=Formula Scout|language=en-GB}}</ref> 

In November, Lindblad joined Prema to compete in the [[2023 Formula 4 South East Asia Championship|Formula 4 South East Asia Championship]] round at the [[Guia Circuit|Macau Grand Prix Circuit]].<ref>{{Cite web|last=Wood|first=Ida|date=25 October 2023|title=Prema to go up against top Asian teams in F4 SEA's Macau races|url=https://formulascout.com/prema-to-go-up-against-top-asian-teams-in-f4-seas-macau-races/112656|access-date=17 February 2025|website=Formula Scout|language=en-GB}}</ref> In a chaotic qualifying, Lindblad was able to secure pole position,<ref>{{Cite web|last=Wood|first=Ida|date=11 November 2023|title=Red Bull junior Lindblad claims F4 pole in chaotic Macau qualifying|url=https://formulascout.com/red-bull-junior-lindblad-claims-f4-pole-in-chaotic-macau-qualifying/113137|access-date=17 February 2025|website=Formula Scout|language=en-GB}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|last=Wood|first=Ida|date=11 November 2023|title=Lindblad "quite surprised by the margin" he took F4 pole by in Macau|url=https://formulascout.com/lindblad-quite-surprised-by-the-margin-he-took-f4-pole-by-in-macau/113141|access-date=17 February 2025|website=Formula Scout|language=en-GB}}</ref> before following it up by winning the qualification race.<ref>{{Cite web|last=Wood|first=Ida|date=12 November 2023|title=Arvid Lindblad wins wet and wild F4 SEA qualification race in Macau|url=https://formulascout.com/arvid-linblad-wins-wet-and-wild-f4-sea-qualification-race-in-macau/113179|access-date=17 February 2025|website=Formula Scout|language=en-GB}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|last=Wood|first=Ida|date=12 November 2023|title=Lindblad: "Macau in the dry is difficult enough", and "bit sketchy" in wet|url=https://formulascout.com/lindblad-macau-in-the-dry-is-difficult-enough-and-bit-sketchy-in-wet/113183|access-date=17 February 2025|website=Formula Scout|language=en-GB}}</ref> His dominance continued the next day, where Lindblad was able to pull away and take home the victory in the main race.<ref>{{Cite web|last=Wood|first=Ida|date=12 November 2023|title=Red Bull junior Arvid Lindblad takes another Macau win in F4 main race|url=https://formulascout.com/red-bull-junior-arvid-lindblad-takes-another-macau-win-in-f4-main-race/113195|access-date=17 February 2025|website=Formula Scout|language=en-GB}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|last=Wood|first=Ida|date=13 November 2023|title=Macau F4 winner Lindblad "gutted" he can't join this weekend's F3 races|url=https://formulascout.com/macau-f4-winner-lindblad-gutted-he-cant-join-this-weekends-f3-races/113198|access-date=17 February 2025|website=Formula Scout|language=en-GB}}</ref> Lindblad's overall performances netted him as a finalist in the [[Autosport BRDC Award|Aston Martin Autosport BRDC Award]] alongside [[Taylor Barnard]], [[Callum Voisin]] and [[Joseph Loake]].<ref>{{Cite web|last=Wood|first=Ida|date=21 September 2023|title=Barnard, Lindblad, Loake and Voisin in Autosport BRDC Award final|url=https://formulascout.com/barnard-lindblad-loake-and-voisin-in-autosport-brdc-award-final/111505|access-date=17 February 2025|website=Formula Scout|language=en-GB}}</ref>

=== Formula Three (2024–2025) ===
==== 2024: Rise to prominence in F3 ====
In the pre-season of 2024, Lindblad signed with [[Mumbai Falcons]] to participate in the first three rounds of the [[2024 Formula Regional Middle East Championship|Formula Regional Middle East Championship]].<ref>{{Cite web|last=Wood|first=Ida|date=8 January 2024|title=Prema reveals it and Mumbai Falcons' line-ups for FRME and F4 UAE|url=https://formulascout.com/prema-reveals-it-and-mumbai-falcons-line-ups-for-frme-and-f4-uae/114757|access-date=17 February 2025|website=Formula Scout|language=en-GB}}</ref> He impressed in the opening round in [[Yas Marina Circuit|Yas Marina]] by winning the second race from reverse pole.<ref>{{Cite web|last=Alonso Lopez|first=Alejandro|date=14 January 2024|title=Lindblad wins in second FRegional Middle East race of 2024|url=https://formulascout.com/lindblad-wins-in-second-fregional-middle-east-race-of-2024/114918|access-date=17 February 2025|website=Formula Scout|language=en-GB}}</ref> Although he only scored three more points in the remaining two rounds, his performances placed him thirteenth overall in the standings.

[[File:2024 Spanish Grand Prix (53810948301).jpg|thumb|left|Lindblad (pictured at [[2024 Barcelona Formula 3 round|Barcelona]]) progressed to [[FIA Formula 3]] in {{FIAF3|2024}} with [[Prema Racing|Prema]].|alt=Lindblad leads the 2024 Barcelona Formula 3 round]]
In October 2023, Lindblad signed to race with [[Prema Racing]] in the [[2024 FIA Formula 3 Championship|FIA Formula 3 Championship]] for 2024, partnering single-seater champions [[Gabriele Minì]] and [[Dino Beganovic]].<ref name=":4">{{Cite web|title=Arvid Lindblad completes PREMA Racing's 2024 roster|date=31 October 2023|url=https://www.fiaformula3.com/Latest/2HlH52QvNxLNaCAU8F7fQK/arvid-lindblad-completes-prema-racings-2024-roster|access-date=31 October 2023|website=FIA_Formula 3® - The Official F3® Website|language=en}}</ref> Qualifying ninth in [[2024 Sakhir Formula 2 round|Bahrain]], Lindblad got off to a great start by winning the sprint race, where he managed his tyres early on before dispatching his rivals in the closing laps and crossing the line five seconds ahead.<ref>{{Cite web |title=Arvid Lindblad takes F3 Sprint Race win on debut |url=https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article/f3-arvid-lindblad-takes-sprint-race-win-on-debut.18p9Skpk3e9DenIWqsMTIh |access-date=2024-12-25 |website=Formula 1® - The Official F1® Website |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|title=Lindblad 'really happy to win on debut' in Bahrain|date=1 March 2024|url=https://feederseries.net/2024/03/01/lindblad-really-happy-to-win-on-debut-in-bahrain/|access-date=17 February 2025|website=Feeder Series|language=en}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|title=RACE ANALYSIS: How rookie Lindblad showed experience beyond his years in Sakhir|date=5 March 2024|url=https://www.fiaformula3.com/Latest/5FxykUeo6IDNivZBAb6iRr/race-analysis-how-rookie-lindblad-showed-experience-beyond-his-years-in|access-date=17 February 2025|website=FIA_Formula 3® - The Official F3® Website|language=en}}</ref> In the feature race, Lindblad finished in a solid eighth place.<ref>{{Cite web|title=R01 Bahrain - FIA Formula 3 Race 2 Report|date=2 March 2024|url=https://premaracing.com/en/news/19267-r01-bahrain-fia-formula-3-race-2-report|access-date=17 February 2025|website=[[Prema Racing]]|language=en}}</ref> He qualified seventh in [[2024 Melbourne Formula 2 round|Melbourne]],<ref>{{Cite web|title=R02 Melbourne - FIA Formula 3 Qualifying Report|date=22 March 2024|url=https://premaracing.com/en/news/19278-r02-melbourne-fia-formula-3-qualifying-report|access-date=17 February 2025|website=[[Prema Racing]]|language=en}}</ref> and put up another overtaking masterclass in the sprint race, enabling him to score a second place podium; he overtook [[Christian Mansell]] and [[Laurens van Hoepen]] but was held at bay by eventual winner [[Martinius Stenshorne]] following a safety car restart.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Suárez |first=Pablo |date=2024-03-23 |title=Stenshorne beats Lindblad to clinch Australia F3 Sprint win |url=https://www.motorsportweek.com/2024/03/23/stenshorne-beats-lindblad-to-clinch-australia-f3-sprint-win/ |access-date=2024-12-25 |website=Motorsport Week |language=en-GB}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|title=Round 2 Post-Sprint Race Press Conference|date=23 March 2024|url=https://www.fiaformula3.com/Latest/5BjZwr0LhhWDCjIQHSoBtC/round-2-post-sprint-race-press-conference|access-date=17 February 2025|website=FIA_Formula 3® - The Official F3® Website|language=en}}</ref> Despite moving up to the top-five in the first half of the race, he struggled with tyres and slipped back to eleventh at the flag.<ref>{{Cite web|title=Lindblad 2nd in Melbourne F3 Sprint – good points for Goethe|date=23 March 2024|url=https://www.redbull.com/int-en/juniorteam/lindblad-2nd-in-melbourne-f3-sprint-%E2%80%93-good-points-for-goethe--2024|access-date=17 February 2025|website=[[Red Bull]]|language=en}}</ref> Lindblad continued to pick up points in [[2024 Imola Formula 3 round|Imola]] where he finished the races in eighth and seventh having qualified fourth.<ref>{{Cite web|title=Goethe takes brilliant 1st & 2nd in Imola F3|date=19 May 2024|url=https://www.redbull.com/int-en/juniorteam/goethe-takes-brilliant-1st-2nd-in-imola-f3|access-date=17 February 2025|website=[[Red Bull]]|language=en}}</ref> Lindblad's first retirement came in the [[2024 Monte Carlo Formula 3 round|Monaco]] sprint race, after he was involved in a multi-car collision on the opening lap.<ref>{{Cite web|title=R04 Monte Carlo - FIA Formula 3 Race 1 Report|date=25 May 2024|url=https://premaracing.com/en/news/19304-r04-monte-carlo-fia-formula-3-race-1-report|access-date=17 February 2025|website=[[Prema Racing]]|language=en}}</ref> The next day however, he secured his best feature race result up to that point with fourth place.<ref>{{Cite web|title=Lindblad happy with building momentum after P4 Monte Carlo finish|date=27 May 2024|url=https://www.fiaformula3.com/Latest/3HQgDnGBlglONR3So6TtLR/lindblad-happy-with-building-momentum-after-p4-monte-carlo-finish|access-date=17 February 2025|website=FIA_Formula 3® - The Official F3® Website|language=en}}</ref> Lindblad secured a best qualifying result in [[2024 Barcelona Formula 3 round|Barcelona]] with a front row start.<ref>{{Cite web|title=Round 5 Post Qualifying Press Conference|date=21 June 2024|url=https://www.fiaformula3.com/Latest/4vOx0rnGGK53kr0dGGRzQ4/round-5-post-qualifying-press-conference|access-date=17 February 2025|website=FIA_Formula 3® - The Official F3® Website|language=en}}</ref> After finishing ninth in the sprint race,<ref>{{Cite web|title=R05 Barcelona - FIA Formula 3 Race 1 Report|date=22 June 2024|url=https://premaracing.com/en/news/19320-r05-barcelona-fia-formula-3-race-1-report|access-date=17 February 2025|website=[[Prema Racing]]|language=en}}</ref> Lindblad overtook polesitter Mansell on lap 4 of the feature race and dominated from there onwards, becoming the youngest feature race winner in FIA F3 history.<ref>{{Cite web |title=Lindblad wins F3's 100th race in Barcelona |url=https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article/f3-lindblad-wins-100th-race-in-championships-history-in-barcelona.1KvsbhBovSyMGdXaGTA0cK |access-date=2024-12-25 |website=Formula 1® - The Official F1® Website |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|title=Round 5 Post Feature Race Thoughts from the Top 3|date=23 June 2024|url=https://www.fiaformula3.com/Latest/7HSeFsXD1IDFtkOizZODpv/round-5-post-feature-race-press-conference|access-date=17 February 2025|website=FIA_Formula 3® - The Official F3® Website|language=en}}</ref> His good qualifying continued into [[2024 Spielberg Formula 3 round|Austria]] where he secured another front row.<ref>{{Cite web|title=Round 6 Post Qualifying Press Conference|date=28 June 2024|url=https://www.fiaformula3.com/Latest/6fAhj4XRswNkPFMwTKdBH3/round-6-post-qualifying-press-conference|access-date=18 February 2025|website=FIA_Formula 3® - The Official F3® Website|language=en}}</ref> He retired from the sprint race due to a puncture sustained in a battle with [[Sami Meguetounif]] whilst fighting just outside the points.<ref>{{Cite web|title=R06 Spielberg - FIA Formula 3 Race 1 Report|date=29 June 2024|url=https://premaracing.com/en/news/19328-r06-spielberg-fia-formula-3-race-1-report|access-date=18 February 2025|website=[[Prema Racing]]|language=en}}</ref> Lindblad also suffered contact from [[Alex Dunne]] which caused him to drop to seventh place.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Waring |first=Bethonie |date=2024-06-30 |title=Browning returns to the FIA F3 lead with Austria feature race win |url=https://formulascout.com/browning-returns-to-the-fia-f3-lead-with-austria-feature-race-win/120758 |access-date=2024-12-25 |website=Formula Scout |language=en-US}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|title=Goethe, Lindblad & Tramnitz all with F3 points in Spielberg|date=30 June 2024|url=https://www.redbull.com/int-en/juniorteam/spielberg-f3|access-date=18 February 2025|website=[[Red Bull]]|language=en}}</ref> 

[[File:2024 FIA Formula 3 Silverstone (54042746099).jpg|thumb|right|Lindblad completed his maiden double victory at [[2024 Silverstone Formula 3 round|Silverstone]], on his way to fourth in the standings.|alt=Lindblad driving the Dallara F3 2019 at the 2024 Silverstone Formula 3 round]]
[[2024 Silverstone Formula 3 round|Silverstone]] became a standout for Lindblad, who first dominantly won the sprint race after taking the lead from [[Noel León]] at the start.<ref>{{Cite web|title=SPRINT RACE: Home favourite Lindblad dominates to take victory at Silverstone|date=6 July 2024|url=https://www.fiaformula3.com/Latest/1N8C3XQERdeVunMptLys7W/sprint-race-home-favourite-lindblad-dominates-to-take-victory-at-silverstone|access-date=18 February 2025|website=FIA_Formula 3® - The Official F3® Website|language=en}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|title=Silverstone sprint winner Lindblad: Results are helping "build confidence"|date=6 July 2024|url=https://feederseries.net/2024/07/06/silverstone-sprint-winner-lindblad-results-are-helping-build-confidence/|access-date=18 February 2025|website=Feeder Series|language=en}}</ref> The next day, Lindblad made the correct decision to pit for dry tyres during the formation lap on a wet but drying track; progressing to second from where he would inherit the feature race win following a penalty for [[Callum Voisin]].<ref>{{Cite web |last=Spadi |first=Daniele |date=2024-07-11 |title=Lindblad does the double as Minì takes championship lead: F3 Silverstone recap |url=https://feederseries.net/2024/07/11/lindblad-does-the-double-as-mini-takes-championship-lead-f3-silverstone-recap/ |access-date=2024-12-25 |website=Feeder Series |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|last=Wood|first=Ida|date=9 July 2024|title=Lindblad "over the moon, don't think I've been this happy in a long time"|url=https://formulascout.com/lindblad-over-the-moon-dont-think-ive-been-this-happy-in-a-long-time/121189|access-date=18 February 2025|website=Formula Scout|language=en-GB}}</ref> In winning both races, Lindblad became the first driver in FIA F3 history to do the double — win both races of a two-race weekend — and put himself into second in the championship with three rounds remaining.<ref>{{Cite web |title=F3: Arvid Lindblad completes historic home soil double |url=https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article/f3-lindblad-completes-historic-home-soil-double-in-frenetic-silverstone.2EQX3kPFzLQtRAXndgcl3g |access-date=2024-12-25 |website=Formula 1® - The Official F1® Website |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|title=Arvid Lindblad's Silverstone Weekend in his Words|date=10 July 2024|url=https://www.fiaformula3.com/Latest/3uoUtgnO3hkeglNX6nDNFX/arvid-lindblads-silverstone-weekend-in-his-words|access-date=18 February 2025|website=FIA_Formula 3® - The Official F3® Website|language=en}}</ref> However, this would be Lindblad's last points finish of the season as a string of poor qualifying results at [[2024 Budapest Formula 3 round|Hungary]], [[2024 Spa-Francorchamps Formula 3 round|Spa]], and [[2024 Monza Formula 3 round|Monza]] contributed to finishes outside the top ten. Race-ending incidents with [[Matías Zagazeta]] and [[Christian Mansell]] contributed to his non-scores in the former two feature races. Additionally, a collision with Voisin in the last-named round, led to a penalty that demoted Lindblad from ninth to 16th in the feature race.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Wood |first=Ida |date=2024-09-01 |title=Mini's title loss followed up by disqualification from FIA F3 finale |url=https://formulascout.com/mini-follows-up-title-loss-with-disqualification-from-f3-finale/123209 |access-date=2024-12-25 |website=Formula Scout |language=en-US}}</ref> Despite dropping to fourth in the standings, Lindblad ended the season as the highest-scoring rookie and helped Prema to win the teams' championship for a third successive year.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Turner |first=Tori |date=2024-09-06 |title=The notable drives you may have missed from F3's Monza title decider |url=https://feederseries.net/2024/09/06/the-notable-drives-you-may-have-missed-from-f3s-monza-title-decider/ |access-date=2024-12-25 |website=Feeder Series |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|title=Arvid Lindblad 2024 Season Review: A record-breaking rookie year|date=24 October 2024|url=https://www.fiaformula3.com/Latest/CznBfrArhKGA2027HGdiI/arvid-lindblad-2024-season-review-a-record-breaking-rookie-year|access-date=18 February 2025|website=FIA_Formula 3® - The Official F3® Website|language=en}}</ref> Lindblad was again selected as a finalist for the [[Autosport BRDC Award|Aston Martin Autosport BRDC Award]] for 2024, alongside [[Freddie Slater (racing driver)|Freddie Slater]], [[Louis Sharp]] and [[Deagen Fairclough]].<ref>{{Cite web|last=Wood|first=Ida|date=26 September 2024|title=Fairclough, Lindblad, Sharp and Slater in Autosport BRDC Award final|url=https://formulascout.com/fairclough-lindlad-sharp-and-slater-in-autosport-brdc-award-final/124240|access-date=18 February 2025|website=Formula Scout|language=en-GB}}</ref>

==== 2025: Maiden title in Formula Regional Oceania ====
In preparation for his [[2025 Formula 2 Championship|Formula 2]] campaign in 2025, Lindblad competed in the [[2025 Formula Regional Oceania Championship|Formula Regional Oceania Championship]] with [[M2 Competition]].<ref>{{Cite web|last=Allen|first=Peter|date=27 December 2024|title=Arvid Lindblad to race in Formula Regional Oceania|url=https://formulascout.com/arvid-lindblad-to-race-in-formula-regional-oceania/127168|access-date=27 December 2024|website=Formula Scout|language=en-GB}}</ref> He started the year off with three podiums in all three races at the season opener at [[Taupo International Motorsport Park]], which included a pole position and win in the third race.<ref>{{Cite web |last=McClure |first=Michael |date=13 January 2025 |title=Feeder Series weekend review: 10–12 January |url=https://feederseries.net/2025/01/13/feeder-series-weekend-review-10-12-january/ |access-date=10 February 2025 |website=Feeder Series |language=en}}</ref> Lindblad continued his podium streak at [[Hampton Downs Motorsport Park|Hampton Downs]], this time scoring two poles and two victories in races 1 and 3 respectively, while he finished the second race in third.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Lau |first=Kaylene |date=20 January 2025 |title=Feeder Series weekend review: 17–19 January |url=https://feederseries.net/2025/01/20/feeder-series-weekend-review-17-19-january/ |access-date=10 February 2025 |website=Feeder Series |language=en}}</ref>

Lindblad won the first race at [[Manfeild: Circuit Chris Amon|Manfeild]], but his seven-race podium streak came to an end during a wet second race, finishing in fourteenth place following a [[safety car]] restart.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Wood |first=Ida |date=26 January 2025 |title=Scoular slices into Lindblad's FRegional Oceania lead with Manfeild win |url=https://formulascout.com/scoular-slices-into-lindblads-fregional-oceania-lead-with-manfeild-win/127914 |access-date=10 February 2025 |website=Formula Scout |language=en-US}}</ref> He bounced back in the third race to take his fifth pole and win of the year, expanding his gap to 40 points from nearest rival [[Nikita Johnson]].<ref>{{Cite web |last=Lau |first=Kaylene |date=27 January 2025 |title=Feeder Series weekend review: 22–26 January |url=https://feederseries.net/2025/01/27/feeder-series-weekend-review-22-26-january/ |access-date=10 February 2025 |website=Feeder Series |language=en}}</ref> During race 1 of the [[Teretonga Park]] round, Lindblad achieved pole position and the fastest lap, finishing in second place behind teammate [[Matías Zagazeta]].<ref>{{Cite web |last=Wood |first=Ida |date=1 February 2025 |title=Zagazeta wins FRegional Oceania's shortened first Teretonga race |url=https://formulascout.com/zagazeta-wins-fregional-oceanias-shortened-first-teretonga-race/128010 |access-date=10 February 2025 |website=Formula Scout |language=en-US}}</ref> Lindblad came in sixth during race 2 and claimed another victory in race 3, expanding his championship margin to 59 points ahead of Johnson.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Lau |first=Kaylene |date=3 February 2025 |title=Feeder Series weekend review: 31 January–02 February |url=https://feederseries.net/2025/02/03/feeder-series-weekend-review-31-january-02-february/ |access-date=10 February 2025 |website=Feeder Series |language=en}}</ref> 

Lindblad clinched the championship at [[Highlands Motorsport Park]], finishing the race in second place, due to the fact that he finished ahead of rivals Johnson and [[Zack Scoular]].<ref name=":5">{{Cite web |last=Lau |first=Kaylene |date=9 February 2025 |title=How Lindblad made the difference in title-winning FR Oceania campaign |url=https://feederseries.net/2025/02/09/how-lindblad-made-the-difference-in-title-winning-fr-oceania-campaign/ |access-date=10 February 2025 |website=Feeder Series |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Wood |first=Ida |date=8 February 2025 |title=Heuzenroeder wins as Lindblad takes title in FRegional Oceania race one |url=https://formulascout.com/heuzenroeder-wins-as-lindblad-takes-title-in-fregional-oceania-race-one/128151 |access-date=10 February 2025 |website=Formula Scout |language=en-US}}</ref> Lindblad retired from race 2 after he was caught in an opening crash involving Zagazeta, [[Patrick Heuzenroeder]], and [[Michael Shin]].<ref name=":5" /><ref>{{Cite web |last=Wood |first=Ida |date=8 February 2025 |title=Johnson wins FRegional Oceania race which starts with huge crash |url=https://formulascout.com/johnson-wins-fregional-oceania-race-which-starts-with-huge-crash/128189 |access-date=10 February 2025 |website=Formula Scout |language=en-US}}</ref> Lindblad bounced back during the season-ending [[2025 New Zealand Grand Prix|New Zealand Grand Prix]], finishing third. Overall, Lindblad finished the season with six wins and 370 points. Additionally, he was able to gain 18 points for his [[FIA Super Licence]] for winning the championship.<ref name=":5" /><ref>{{Cite web |last=McClure |first=Michael |date=10 February 2025 |title=Feeder Series weekend review, results and standings: 07–09 February |url=https://feederseries.net/2025/02/10/feeder-series-weekend-review-07-09-february/ |access-date=10 February 2025 |website=Feeder Series |language=en}}</ref>

=== FIA Formula 2 (2025) ===
[[File:FIA F2 Austria 2025 Nr. 4 Lindblad.jpg|thumb|left|Lindblad contested [[FIA Formula 2]] in {{F2|2025}}, becoming the youngest race winner in [[Formula Two]] history, aged 17.|alt=Lindblad driving the Dallara F2 2024 at the 2025 Spielberg Formula 2 round]]
In September 2024, Lindblad announced that he would be promoted to [[FIA Formula 2]] with [[Campos Racing]] for {{F2|2025}}.<ref>{{Cite web|title=Arvid Lindblad graduates to F2 with Campos Racing for 2025|date=12 September 2024|url=https://www.fiaformula2.com/Latest/3xjrtzZ67bwpE0qV3fdFtt/arvid-lindblad-graduates-to-f2-with-campos-racing-for-2025|access-date=12 September 2024|website=FIA_F2® - The Official F2® Website|language=en}}</ref> Ahead of the season, Lindblad remarked that he was "filled with confidence" and anticipated a "really big challenge".<ref>{{Cite web|title=Lindblad ‘super excited’ to step up to F2 with Campos as 2025 preparations begin|date=25 September 2024|url=https://www.fiaformula2.com/Latest/7oGskMMz2Gn24f6SPvb7kJ/lindblad-super-excited-to-step-up-to-f2-with-campos-as-2025-preparations|access-date=3 January 2026|website=FIA_F2® - The Official F2® Website|language=en}}</ref> After finishing just outside the points during the [[2025 Melbourne Formula 2 round|Melbourne sprint]],<ref>{{Cite web|title=Pepe Martí Scores Points in a Chaotic Season Opener in Melbourne|date=17 March 2025|url=https://www.camposracing.com/en/noticias/fia-f2/pepe-marti-scores-points-in-a-chaotic-season-opener-in-melbourne|access-date=3 January 2026|website=[[Campos Racing]]|language=en}}</ref> he had an improved performance in [[2025 Sakhir Formula 2 round|Bahrain]] despite qualifying sixteenth, making up positions to finish fifth in the [[FIA Formula 2 Championship#Race weekend|sprint race]] and eighth in the [[FIA Formula 2 Championship#Race weekend|feature]].<ref>{{Cite web|title=4 things we learned from the 2025 Bahrain F2 round|date=14 April 2025|url=https://feederseries.net/2025/04/14/4-things-we-learned-from-the-2025-bahrain-f2-round/|access-date=3 January 2026|website=Feeder Series|language=en}}</ref> In [[2025 Jeddah Formula 2 round|Jeddah]], Lindblad qualified fifth.<ref>{{Cite web|title=Lindblad hopeful of a double podium after qualifying fifth in Jeddah|date=18 April 2025|url=https://www.fiaformula2.com/Latest/2eT4Etg4lnD0SuoVR79m9p/lindblad-hopeful-of-a-double-podium-after-qualifying-fifth-in-jeddah|access-date=3 January 2026|website=FIA_F2® - The Official F2® Website|language=en}}</ref> After benefitting from a mistake from [[Pepe Martí]], Lindblad went on to finish second on the road, but was promoted to the win after [[Richard Verschoor]] was penalised.{{Efn|Lindblad's age was incorrectly stated as 17 years and 243 days in initial reports.<ref>{{cite web |last=Gray |first=Andy |date=19 April 2025 |title=Lindblad makes F2 history as Dunne leads standings |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/motorsport/articles/c2ewpwv802po |website=[[BBC Sport]] |publisher=[[BBC]] |access-date=6 June 2025}}</ref>}} This made Lindblad the youngest Formula 2 winner in history at 17 years and 254 days.<ref>{{Cite web|title=The path Lindblad took to earn his 2026 Racing Bulls F1 seat|url=https://feederseries.net/2025/12/02/the-path-lindblad-took-to-earn-his-2026-racing-bulls-f1-seat/|website=Feeder Series|date=2025-12-02|access-date=2025-12-02|language=en|first=Martin|last=Lloyd|first2=Calla|last2=Kra-Caskey|last3=McClure|first3=Michael}}</ref> In the feature race, he finished seventh.<ref>{{Cite web|title=What We Learned: A few talking points from Round 3 in Jeddah|date=24 April 2025|url=https://www.fiaformula2.com/Latest/eXKCCSdyzavn8LK5hbrNW/what-we-learned-a-few-talking-points-from-round-3-in-jeddah|access-date=3 January 2026|website=FIA_F2® - The Official F2® Website|language=en}}</ref> He qualified sixth in [[2025 Imola Formula 2 round|Imola]],<ref>{{Cite web|title=Lindblad says Campos are ‘in a good window’ after competitive Imola Qualifying|date=16 May 2025|url=https://www.fiaformula2.com/Latest/7g3UPOi9w3ZjIXsrw5qbiH/lindblad-says-campos-in-a-good-window-after-competitive-imola-qualifying|access-date=4 January 2026|website=FIA_F2® - The Official F2® Website|language=en}}</ref> and finished in second during the sprint following a strong start.<ref>{{Cite web|title=Round 4 Post Sprint Race Press Conference|date=17 May 2025|url=https://www.fiaformula2.com/Latest/28yIqnkL2cJkULgLWeZUQD/round-4-post-sprint-race-press-conference|access-date=4 January 2026|website=FIA_F2® - The Official F2® Website|language=en}}</ref> A slow stop during the pit cycle dropped Lindblad out of podium contention in the feature race, which he placed fourth.<ref>{{Cite web|title=Looking quick but with no luck: Arvid Lindblad’s weekend debrief|date=20 May 2025|url=https://www.fiaformula2.com/Latest/79iJIcAqNybOPSEW5vhW4M/looking-quick-but-with-no-luck-arvid-lindblads-weekend-debrief|access-date=4 January 2026|website=FIA_F2® - The Official F2® Website|language=en}}</ref> In [[2025 Monte Carlo Formula 2 round|Monaco]], Lindblad received a ten-second penalty for causing a collision with [[Jak Crawford]], this dropped him off the podium to eighth.<ref>{{Cite web|title=Monaco F2 sprint race winner Maini: ‘I never thought I’d be here’|date=24 May 2025|url=https://feederseries.net/2025/05/24/monaco-f2-sprint-race-winner-maini-i-never-thought-id-be-here/|access-date=4 January 2026|website=Feeder Series|language=en}}</ref> History repeated itself the next day as he was set to finish third during the feature race, but dropped to fifth after a penalty for speeding in the pit lane.<ref>{{Cite web|title=Lindblad keeps cool in Monaco F2 mayhem|date=26 May 2025|url=https://www.redbull.com/int-en/juniorteam/lindblad-keeps-cool-in-monaco-f2-mayhem-2025|access-date=4 January 2026|website=[[Red Bull]]|language=en}}</ref> [[2025 Barcelona Formula 2 round|Barcelona]] became a standout for Lindblad, as he claimed pole position became the second-youngest [[polesitter]] in F2 history behind [[Théo Pourchaire]].<ref>{{Cite web|title=Barcelona|date=30 May 2025|url=https://www.fiaformula2.com/Results?raceid=1083|access-date=30 May 2025|website=FIA_F2® - The Official F2® Website|language=en}}</ref> After finishing eighth in the sprint despite a tangle with [[Richard Verschoor]],<ref>{{Cite web|title=Lindblad Shines in Barcelona as Campos Racing Retakes Teams’ Championship Lead|date=2 June 2025|url=https://www.camposracing.com/en/noticias/fia-f2/lindblad-shines-in-barcelona-as-campos-racing-retakes-teams-championship-lead|access-date=4 January 2026|website=[[Campos Racing]]|language=en}}</ref> he successfully converted his pole to feature race victory in his team's home race.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Kra-Caskey |first=Calla |date=2025-06-01 |title=Lindblad sails to victory on Campos' home soil under safety car finish |url=https://feederseries.net/2025/06/01/lindblad-sails-to-victory-on-campos-home-soil-under-safety-car-finish/|access-date=2025-06-02 |website=Feeder Series |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|title=Round 6 Post Feature Race Press Conference|date=1 June 2025|url=https://www.fiaformula2.com/Latest/6bJo8GkM4UkDRwFmzLHC8a/round-6-post-feature-race-press-conference|access-date=4 January 2026|website=FIA_F2® - The Official F2® Website|language=en}}</ref>

A challenging patch of form followed starting from [[2025 Spielberg Formula 2 round|Austria]], where he scored no points after collisions with [[Luke Browning]] and [[Oliver Goethe]] in the sprint and feature race respectively,<ref>{{Cite web|title=5 things we learned from the 2025 Spielberg F2 round|date=1 July 2025|url=https://feederseries.net/2025/07/01/5-things-we-learned-from-the-2025-spielberg-f2-round/|access-date=5 January 2026|website=Feeder Series|language=en}}</ref> and finished eighth in a wet [[2025 Silverstone Formula 2 round|Silverstone feature race]].<ref>{{Cite web|title=Lindblad and Martí salvage valuable points to keep Campos Racing on top|date=7 July 2025|url=https://www.camposracing.com/en/noticias/fia-f2/lindblad-and-marti-salvage-valuable-points-to-keep-campos-racing-on-top|access-date=5 January 2026|website=[[Campos Racing]]|language=en}}</ref> He qualified fifth in [[2025 Spa-Francorchamps Formula 2 round|Spa-Francorchamps]], and made his way to second in a damp feature race,<ref>{{Cite web|title=Round 9 Post Feature Race Press Conference|date=27 July 2025|url=https://www.fiaformula2.com/Latest/2EjGd7jxaV5CswSEX8NUOm/round-9-post-feature-race-press-conference|access-date=5 January 2026|website=FIA_F2® - The Official F2® Website|language=en}}</ref> but was disqualified for illegal tyre pressures.<ref>{{Cite web|title=Arvid Lindblad disqualified following Spa Francorchamps Feature Race|date=27 July 2025|url=https://www.fiaformula2.com/Latest/Gho0uyx2obcAGnVY92Ds9/arvid-lindblad-disqualified-following-spa-francorchamps-feature-race|access-date=5 January 2026|website=FIA_F2® - The Official F2® Website|language=en}}</ref> In [[2025 Budapest Formula 2 round|Budapest]], Lindblad was embroiled in a contentious battle with teammate Martí, but struggled with tyres late on and finished fourth, but dropped to tenth after a penalty for leaving the track and gaining an advantage.<ref>{{Cite web|title=Lindblad and Browning penalised following Budapest Sprint Race|date=2 August 2025|url=https://www.fiaformula2.com/Latest/3619RTey5FcH9K16aHwRJb/lindblad-and-browning-penalised-following-budapest-sprint-race|access-date=5 January 2026|website=FIA_F2® - The Official F2® Website|language=en}}</ref> He finished sixth in the feature race on the alternate strategy.<ref>{{Cite web|title=Pepe Martí Returns to Sprint Race Victory in Hungary; Lindblad Scores Points on Sunday|date=4 August 2025|url=https://www.camposracing.com/en/noticias/fia-f2/pepe-marti-returns-to-sprint-race-victory-in-hungary-lindblad-scores-points-on-sunday|access-date=5 January 2026|website=[[Campos Racing]]|language=en}}</ref> Lindblad returned to the podium during the sprint race in [[2025 Monza Formula 2 round|Monza]], finishing second,<ref>{{Cite web|title=Round 11 Post Sprint Race Press Conference|date=6 September 2025|url=https://www.fiaformula2.com/Latest/4jjW6lLkyTe4JMwfiglKQ6/round-11-post-sprint-race-press-conference|access-date=5 January 2026|website=FIA_F2® - The Official F2® Website|language=en}}</ref> but was criticised for his collisions during the feature race with [[Alex Dunne]] and [[Roman Staněk]], earning Lindblad a ten-place grid penalty for the [[2025 Baku Formula 2 round|Baku sprint race]].<ref>{{Cite web|title=Lindblad penalised following Monza Feature Race|date=7 September 2025|url=https://www.fiaformula2.com/Latest/5lHdYldNY7sNNRWOAorR2V/lindblad-penalised-following-monza-feature-race|access-date=5 January 2026|website=FIA_F2® - The Official F2® Website|language=en}}</ref> He did not fare much better there, although he managed a sixth place finish in the feature race.<ref>{{Cite web|title=Lindblad satisfied with Baku comeback drive to P6 after difficult weekend|date=23 September 2025|url=https://www.fiaformula2.com/Latest/1htZ7H3g2T6J10r6QyCgsq/lindblad-satisfied-with-baku-comeback-drive-to-p6-after-difficult-weekend|access-date=5 January 2026|website=FIA_F2® - The Official F2® Website|language=en}}</ref> Lindblad qualified seventeenth in [[2025 Lusail Formula 2 round|Qatar]], but he finished fourth in the feature race after a gamble to fit softs early on the alternate strategy despite a post-race investigation.<ref>{{Cite web|title=Arvid Lindblad retains P4 following post Lusail Feature Race investigation|date=30 November 2025|url=https://www.fiaformula2.com/Latest/1RrFNmyxrb0amoPnIR21He/arvid-lindblad-retains-p4-following-post-lusail-feature-race-investigation|access-date=5 January 2026|website=FIA_F2® - The Official F2® Website|language=en}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|title=Lindblad pleased with ‘gamble’ and Lusail recovery with Campos|date=1 December 2025|url=https://www.fiaformula2.com/Latest/4wW0mn0qWP6NLukD3qRzqC/lindblad-pleased-with-gamble-and-lusail-recovery-with-campos|access-date=5 January 2026|website=FIA_F2® - The Official F2® Website|language=en}}</ref> [[2025 Yas Island Formula 2 round|Abu Dhabi]] provided one last hurrah for Lindblad in the sprint, as he held off [[Joshua Dürksen]] to take his third win of the campaign from reverse pole.<ref>{{Cite web|title=SPRINT RACE: Lindblad holds off Duerksen to claim victory at Yas Marina|date=6 December 2025|url=https://www.fiaformula2.com/Latest/4DIIFB1ye6QeGAL8utoPUi/sprint-race-lindblad-holds-off-duerksen-to-claim-victory-at-yas-marina|access-date=5 January 2026|website=FIA_F2® - The Official F2® Website|language=en}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|last=Alleb|first=Peter|date=20 December 2025|title=Lindblad “not super happy” with F2 season despite reaching F1 goal|url=https://formulascout.com/lindblad-not-super-happy-with-f2-season-despite-reaching-f1-goal/136869|access-date=5 January 2026|website=Formula Scout|language=en-GB}}</ref> An early safety car in the feature race compromised his alternate strategy, but he still salvaged a ninth place finish.<ref>{{Cite web|title=Lindblad Ends the Year with Victory as Tsolov Takes His First Podium in the Category|date=8 December 2025|url=https://www.camposracing.com/en/noticias/fia-f2/lindblad-ends-the-year-with-victory-as-tsolov-takes-his-first-podium-in-the-category|access-date=5 January 2026|website=[[Campos Racing]]|language=en}}</ref> Lindblad finished the season sixth in the standings on 134 points with three wins from five podiums.<ref>{{Cite web|title=Campos Racing 2025 Season Review: Helping drivers achieve their goal|date=29 December 2025|url=https://www.fiaformula2.com/Latest/DiLLUxysSMtgFMxyS7gp0/campos-racing-2025-season-review-helping-drivers-achieve-their-goal|access-date=5 January 2026|website=FIA_F2® - The Official F2® Website|language=en}}</ref>

== Formula One career ==
[[File:Arvid Lindblad at the Red Bull Fan Zone – Crown Riverwalk, Melbourne (028A7727).jpg|thumb|right|Lindblad (pictured in 2026) joined the [[Red Bull Junior Team]] in [[kart racing]] at the age of 13 and became a [[test driver]] for both [[Red Bull GmbH|Red Bull]] teams three years later.|alt=Lindblad smiling and waving in Racing Bulls team merchandise]]
For his 2021 campaign in [[kart racing]], aged 13, Lindblad joined the [[Red Bull Junior Team]] as a [[Red Bull GmbH|Red Bull]]–supported driver, later becoming a full member ahead of his [[Formula 4]] debut in 2022.<ref name="SIL2026">{{Cite web |url=https://www.silverstone.co.uk/news/arvid-lindblads-journey-formula-1 |title=Arvid Lindblad's Journey to Formula 1 |date=5 January 2026 |website=[[Silverstone Circuit]] |publisher=[[British Racing Drivers' Club]] |access-date=8 March 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260308011625/https://www.silverstone.co.uk/news/arvid-lindblads-journey-formula-1 |archive-date=8 March 2026 |url-status=live}}</ref> He first drove a [[Formula One car]] in September 2024, completing a show-run in the [[Red Bull RB8]] in [[Houston]].<ref>{{Cite news |url=https://www.houstonchronicle.com/news/houston-texas/trending/article/red-bull-showrun-showcase-f1-19743187.php |url-access=subscription |title=Racing fans treated to lively Red Bull Showrun showcase in downtown Houston |last=Warren |first=Peter |date=7 September 2024 |work=[[Houston Chronicle]] |publisher=[[Hearst Communications]] |access-date=8 March 2026 |issn=1074-7109 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260213112627/https://www.houstonchronicle.com/news/houston-texas/trending/article/red-bull-showrun-showcase-f1-19743187.php |archive-date=13 February 2026 |url-status=live}}</ref> Five months later, he conducted his maiden private test with [[Racing Bulls]] in the [[AlphaTauri AT04|AT04]] at [[Imola Circuit|Imola]], which he repeated in June alongside [[Ayumu Iwasa]].<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.autosport.com/f1/news/f1-lindblad-laps-imola-in-at04-training-for-fp1-debut/10735474/ |title=Lindblad turns laps at Imola in first proper F1 test |last=Rava |first=Jacopo |date=23 June 2025 |website=[[Autosport]] |publisher=[[Motorsport Network]] |access-date=8 March 2026 |issn=0269-946X |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250623133207/https://www.autosport.com/f1/news/f1-lindblad-laps-imola-in-at04-training-for-fp1-debut/10735474/ |archive-date=23 June 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref> He raced against three on-foot [[Leeds United F.C.]] players—[[Willy Gnonto]], [[Largie Ramazani]], and [[Isaac Schmidt]]—at [[Elland Road]] that month in the [[Red Bull RB7|RB7]].<ref>{{Cite news |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/football/articles/c15nd58y0wjo |title=Leeds can't win every race... |date=4 June 2025 |work=[[BBC Sport]] |publisher=[[BBC]] |access-date=5 June 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250605135150/https://www.bbc.com/sport/football/articles/c15nd58y0wjo |archive-date=5 June 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref>

Upon request from Red Bull, Lindblad was granted an [[FIA Super License]] aged 17, similar to the request approved for [[Kimi Antonelli]] in 2024.<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.espn.co.uk/f1/story/_/id/45484762/arvid-lindblad-17-gets-f1-exemption-red-bull-request |title=Arvid Lindblad, 17, gets F1 exemption after Red Bull request |last=Edmondson |first=Laurence |date=10 June 2025 |website=[[ESPN]] |publisher=[[ESPN Inc.]] |access-date=8 March 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250701130613/https://www.espn.co.uk/f1/story/_/id/45484762/arvid-lindblad-17-gets-f1-exemption-red-bull-request |archive-date=1 July 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref> He made his [[free practice]] debut for [[Red Bull Racing|Red Bull]] at the {{F1GP|2025|British}}, where he set the fourteenth-fastest time in place of [[Yuki Tsunoda]].<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article/lindblad-reflects-on-amazing-fp1-debut-with-red-bull-at-silverstone.1osPzRxLa3iq9ff6n7OKQf |title=Lindblad reflects on 'amazing' FP1 debut with Red Bull at Silverstone |date=4 July 2025 |website=[[Formula 1]] |publisher=[[Formula One Group]] |access-date=8 March 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260120091921/https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article/lindblad-reflects-on-amazing-fp1-debut-with-red-bull-at-silverstone.1osPzRxLa3iq9ff6n7OKQf |archive-date=20 January 2026 |url-status=live}}</ref> He made a further practice appearance for Red Bull in [[2025 Mexico City Grand Prix|Mexico City]] in place of [[Max Verstappen]], where he placed sixth and impressed Red Bull with his pace and technical feedback.<ref name="SIL2026"/><ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.autosport.com/f1/news/how-lindblad-impressed-red-bull-bosses-in-mexico-gp-fp1-outing/10770875/ |title=How Lindblad impressed Red Bull bosses in Mexico GP FP1 outing |last1=Codling |first1=Stuart |last2=Vording |first2=Ronald |date=24 October 2025 |website=[[Autosport]] |publisher=[[Motorsport Network]] |access-date=8 March 2026 |issn=0269-946X |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20251025074922/https://www.autosport.com/f1/news/how-lindblad-impressed-red-bull-bosses-in-mexico-gp-fp1-outing/10770875/ |archive-date=25 October 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref> He again replaced Tsunoda during free practice of the season-ending {{F1GP|2025|Abu Dhabi}}, ending fifteenth overall.<ref name="SIL2026"/> He joined Racing Bulls for the post-season test, where his running was cut short due to a mechanical issue.<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.the-race.com/formula-1/everything-we-learned-from-f1s-first-2026-test/ |title=Everything we learned from F1's first '2026' test |last1=Straw |first1=Edd |last2=Mitchell-Malm |first2=Scott |date=9 December 2025 |website=The Race |publisher=The Race Media |access-date=8 March 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260117171006/https://www.the-race.com/formula-1/everything-we-learned-from-f1s-first-2026-test/ |archive-date=17 January 2026 |url-status=live}}</ref>

=== Racing Bulls (2026) ===
[[File:Liam Lawson and Arvid Lindblad at the Red Bull Fan Zone – Crown Riverwalk, Melbourne (028A7784).jpg|thumb|left|Lindblad ''(right)'' debuted in Formula One with [[Racing Bulls]] at the {{F1GP|2026|Australian}} in {{F1|2026}}, partnering [[Liam Lawson]].|alt=Lindblad and Liam Lawson, holding a microphone, looking to the side and smiling at a press event for the 2026 Australian Grand Prix]]
[[File:FIA F1 Austria 2026 Nr. 41 Lindblad (3).jpg|thumb|Lindblad driving the [[Racing Bulls VCARB 03|VCARB 03]] at the [[2026 Austrian Grand Prix]]]]
In December 2025, Lindblad signed for [[Racing Bulls]]—the sister team of [[Red Bull Racing|Red Bull]]—to replace the promoted [[Isack Hadjar]] and compete alongside third-year [[Liam Lawson]] for [[Regulation changes (2026 Formula One World Championship)|new power unit and chassis regulations]] in {{F1|2026}}.<ref>{{Cite news |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/formula1/articles/c5y0rlx05l4o |title=Hadjar promoted and Lindblad, 18, gets F1 drive |last=Benson |first=Andrew |date=2 December 2025 |work=[[BBC Sport]] |publisher=[[BBC]] |access-date=8 March 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20251225235708/https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/formula1/articles/c5y0rlx05l4o |archive-date=25 December 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref> Aged 18, he became the [[List of Formula One driver records#Youngest drivers to start a race|fourth-youngest driver in Formula One history]] and surpassed [[Oliver Bearman]] as the [[Formula One drivers from the United Kingdom|youngest-ever Briton]]; unsure whether he was "entirely ready" for Formula One, Lindblad insisted he was "used to being thrown in the deep end".<ref name="INDY2026" /><ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.motorsport.com/f1/news/arvid-lindblad-unsure-if-hes-entirely-ready-for-f1-despite-praise-from-racing-bulls/10793599/ |title=Arvid Lindblad unsure if he's "entirely ready" for F1 – despite praise from Racing Bulls |last=Hardy |first=Ed |date=29 January 2026 |website=[[Motorsport.com]] |publisher=[[Motorsport Network]] |access-date=8 March 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260129195313/https://www.motorsport.com/f1/news/arvid-lindblad-unsure-if-hes-entirely-ready-for-f1-despite-praise-from-racing-bulls/10793599/ |archive-date=29 January 2026 |url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.autosport.com/f1/news/lindblad-f1-rookie-racing-bulls/10788243/ |title=Lindblad braced for "difficult" F1 rookie season with Racing Bulls |last=Vinel |first=Ben |date=6 January 2026 |website=[[Autosport]] |publisher=[[Motorsport Network]] |access-date=8 March 2026 |issn=0269-946X |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260308013135/https://www.autosport.com/f1/news/lindblad-f1-rookie-racing-bulls/10788243/ |archive-date=8 March 2026 |url-status=live}}</ref> Racing Bulls emerged as an upper-[[Glossary of motorsport terms#M|midfield]] team with the [[Racing Bulls VCARB 03|VCARB 03]],<ref>{{Cite news |url=https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2026/mar/04/formula-one-2026-team-by-team-guide-cars-drivers-motor-sport |title=Formula One 2026: team-by-team guide to the cars and drivers |last=Richards |first=Giles |date=4 March 2026 |work=[[The Guardian]] |publisher=[[Guardian Media Group]] |access-date=9 March 2026 |issn=1756-3224 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260309031823/https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2026/mar/04/formula-one-2026-team-by-team-guide-cars-drivers-motor-sport |archive-date=9 March 2026 |url-status=live}}</ref> with Lindblad qualifying ninth on debut in [[2026 Australian Grand Prix|Australia]], immediately passing the frontrunners to reach the [[Podium#In motorsport|podium]] positions before settling for eighth as Lawson dropped outside the [[List of Formula One points systems|points]].<ref>{{Cite news |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/formula1/articles/cd9gpzge02lo |title=Brit rookie Lindblad 'living his dream' on F1 debut |last=Chowdhury |first=Tasnim |date=8 March 2026 |work=[[BBC Sport]] |publisher=[[BBC]] |access-date=9 March 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260309031633/https://www.bbc.com/sport/formula1/articles/cd9gpzge02lo |archive-date=9 March 2026 |url-status=live}}</ref> Having retired from the [[Formula One sprint|sprint]], he finished twelfth in [[2026 Chinese Grand Prix|China]] on an alternate strategy.<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.silverstone.co.uk/news/f1-2026-chinese-grand-prix-results-antonelli-seals-first-win-mercedes |title=F1 2026 Chinese Grand Prix results: Antonelli seals first win for Mercedes |date=16 March 2026 |website=[[Silverstone Circuit]] |publisher=[[British Racing Drivers' Club]] |access-date=18 March 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260318112456/https://www.silverstone.co.uk/news/f1-2026-chinese-grand-prix-results-antonelli-seals-first-win-mercedes |archive-date=18 March 2026 |url-status=live}}</ref>

Lindblad placed fourteenth at both the [[2026 Japanese Grand Prix|Japanese Grand Prix]] and the [[2026 Miami Grand Prix|Miami Grand Prix]],<ref>{{Cite web |date=2026-03-28 |title=F1 Results - 2026 Japanese Grand Prix |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/formula1/2026/japanese-grand-prix/results |access-date=2026-07-19 |website=BBC Sport |language=en-GB}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |date=2026-05-01 |title=F1 Results - 2026 Miami Grand Prix |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/formula1/2026/miami-grand-prix/results |access-date=2026-07-19 |website=BBC Sport |language=en-GB}}</ref> before failing to start at the [[2026 Canadian Grand Prix|Canadian Grand Prix]] due to a gearbox issue.<ref>{{Cite web |title=F1 2026 Canadian Grand Prix results: Mercedes clash in Montreal |url=https://www.silverstone.co.uk/news/f1-2026-canadian-grand-prix-results-mercedes-clash-montreal |access-date=2026-07-19 |website=Silverstone |language=en}}</ref> He scored points again with a seventh place finish in [[2026 Monaco Grand Prix|Monaco]],<ref>{{Cite web |date=2026-06-06 |title=F1 Results - 2026 Monaco Grand Prix |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/formula1/2026/monaco-grand-prix/results |access-date=2026-07-19 |website=BBC Sport |language=en-GB}}</ref> a ninth place finish at [[2026 Barcelona-Catalunya Grand Prix|Barcelona-Catalunya]],<ref>{{Cite web |date=2026-06-13 |title=F1 Results - 2026 Catalunya Grand Prix |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/formula1/2026/catalunya-grand-prix/results |access-date=2026-07-19 |website=BBC Sport |language=en-GB}}</ref> and a tenth place finish in [[2026 Austrian Grand Prix|Austria]].<ref>{{Cite web |date=2026-06-27 |title=F1 Results - 2026 Austrian Grand Prix |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/formula1/2026/austrian-grand-prix/results |access-date=2026-07-19 |website=BBC Sport |language=en-GB}}</ref> At his home race in [[2026 British Grand Prix|Silverstone]],<ref>{{Cite web |last=Mandal |first=Anirban Aly |date=2026-06-29 |title=Arvid Lindblad reveals &#8216;childhood dream&#8217; inspired gesture for first home F1 race |url=https://www.motorsportweek.com/2026/06/29/arvid-lindblad-reveals-childhood-dream-inspired-gesture-for-first-home-f1-race/ |access-date=2026-07-19 |website=Motorsport Week |language=en-GB}}</ref> Lindblad placed seventh,<ref>{{Cite web |date=2026-07-03 |title=F1 Results - 2026 British Grand Prix |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/formula1/2026/british-grand-prix/results |access-date=2026-07-19 |website=BBC Sport |language=en-GB}}</ref> followed by a ninth place finish at the [[2026 Belgian Grand Prix|Belgian Grand Prix]].<ref>{{Cite web |date=2026-07-18 |title=F1 Results - 2026 Belgian Grand Prix |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/formula1/2026/belgian-grand-prix/results |access-date=2026-07-19 |website=BBC Sport |language=en-GB}}</ref> He qualified ninth and finished tenth and the [[2026 Hungarian Grand Prix|Hungarian Grand Prix]].<ref>{{Cite web |last=Benson |first=Andrew |date=2026-07-25 |title=Hungarian Grand Prix: Lando Norris takes pole as Lewis Hamilton given three-place grid penalty |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/formula1/articles/c4gv02vyzv4o |access-date=2026-07-26 |website=BBC Sport |language=en-GB}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |date=2026-07-26 |title=F1 2026 Hungarian Grand Prix results |url=https://www.the-race.com/formula-1/f1-2026-hungarian-grand-prix-results/ |access-date=2026-07-26 |website=The Race |language=en}}</ref>

== Personal life ==
Lindblad selected 41 as his [[List of Formula One driver numbers|personal driver number]] in Formula One, its resemblance to his initials, "AL", and lack of strong associations with other sports figures.<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.planetf1.com/news/arvid-lindblad-explains-reasoning-behind-unique-number-f1-debut |title=Why rookie Arvid Lindblad picked rare F1 number 41 for 2026 debut |last=Cooper |first=Sam |date=18 January 2026 |website=PlanetF1 |access-date=8 March 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260202231650/https://www.planetf1.com/news/arvid-lindblad-explains-reasoning-behind-unique-number-f1-debut |archive-date=2 February 2026 |url-status=live}}</ref> His [[racing helmet]] uses shades of fluorescent yellow, teal, and red, featuring the ''[[Tiranga]]'' interposed between the flags [[Flag of England|of England]] and [[Flag of Sweden|Sweden]].<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.planetf1.com/news/f1-driver-helmets-2026-season |title=F1 driver helmets: What designs have been unveiled ahead of the 2026 season? |last=Valantine |first=Henry |date=27 February 2026 |website=PlanetF1 |access-date=8 March 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260217143224/https://www.planetf1.com/news/f1-driver-helmets-2026-season |archive-date=17 February 2026 |url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c0kr27j6z2vo |title=Britain's youngest F1 driver on his debut season so far – and learning to skateboard |last=O'Donnell |first=Áine |date=19 April 2026 |work=[[BBC News]] |publisher=[[BBC]] |access-date=19 April 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260419180435/https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c0kr27j6z2vo |archive-date=19 April 2026 |url-status=live}}</ref> He has been acclaimed by Indian fans as their sole representative in Formula One, where [[Formula One drivers from India|Indian drivers]] have been absent since [[Narain Karthikeyan]] in {{F1|2012}}, and has expressed his desire to see the return of the [[Indian Grand Prix]].<ref>{{Cite news |url=https://gulfnews.com/sport/motorsport/why-indian-expats-in-uae-will-be-cheering-for-new-racing-bulls-driver-arvid-lindblad-1.500369652 |title=Why Indian expats in UAE will be cheering for new Racing Bulls driver Arvid Lindblad |last=Sengupta |first=Jaydip |date=5 December 2025 |work=[[Gulf News]] |publisher=[[Al Nisr Publishing]] |access-date=8 March 2026 |oclc=232115522 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260217110841/https://gulfnews.com/sport/motorsport/why-indian-expats-in-uae-will-be-cheering-for-new-racing-bulls-driver-arvid-lindblad-1.500369652 |archive-date=17 February 2026 |url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news |url=https://www.telegraphindia.com/sports/arvid-lindblad-looks-forward-to-bringing-a-bit-of-india-back-to-the-f1-grid/cid/2149916 |title=Arvid Lindblad looks 'forward to bringing a bit of India back to the F1 grid' |last=Dutta |first=Debayan |date=5 March 2026 |work=[[The Telegraph (India)|The Telegraph]] |publisher=[[ABP Group]] |access-date=8 March 2026 |oclc=271717941 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260308035003/https://www.telegraphindia.com/sports/arvid-lindblad-looks-forward-to-bringing-a-bit-of-india-back-to-the-f1-grid/cid/2149916 |archive-date=8 March 2026 |url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news |url=https://www.indiatoday.in/sports/formula-one/story/arvid-lindblad-brings-f1-excitement-back-to-india-at-red-bull-motojam-2026-in-photos-2878395-2026-03-06 |title=Arvid Lindblad brings F1 excitement back to India at Red Bull Motojam 2026: In Photos |date=6 March 2026 |work=[[India Today]] |publisher=[[Living Media India]] |access-date=8 March 2026 |issn=0254-8399 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260308035024/https://www.indiatoday.in/sports/formula-one/story/arvid-lindblad-brings-f1-excitement-back-to-india-at-red-bull-motojam-2026-in-photos-2878395-2026-03-06 |archive-date=8 March 2026 |url-status=live}}</ref><ref name="RB2026">{{Cite web |url=https://www.redbull.com/in-en/arvid-lindblad-indian-connections |title=Arvid Lindblad, the new poster child of Indian motorsports |last=Sequeira |first=Sean |date=15 January 2026 |website=[[Red Bull]] |publisher=[[Red Bull GmbH]] |access-date=7 March 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260307135320/https://www.redbull.com/in-en/arvid-lindblad-indian-connections/ |archive-date=7 March 2026 |url-status=live}}</ref>

Lindblad cites [[Lewis Hamilton]]—the only [[black people|black]] driver in Formula One history—as his inspiration; he has further noted the "[[Big Three (tennis)|Big Three]]" of men's [[tennis]], [[Michael Phelps]], and [[Michael Jordan]] as his wider sporting idols.<ref name="GQ2026">{{Cite magazine |url=https://www.gq-magazine.co.uk/article/treat-arvid-lindblad-as-the-new-kid-on-the-block-at-your-peril |title=Treat Arvid Lindblad as the new kid on the block at your peril |last=Christensen |first=Mike |date=3 March 2026 |magazine=[[British GQ]] |publisher=[[Condé Nast]] |access-date=8 March 2026 |issn=0954-8750 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260303160858/https://www.gq-magazine.co.uk/article/treat-arvid-lindblad-as-the-new-kid-on-the-block-at-your-peril |archive-date=3 March 2026 |url-status=live}}</ref> Beyond Formula One, he is interested in [[Grand Prix motorcycle racing]], where his favourite rider is [[Marc Márquez]]; [[association football]], where he supports the [[England national football team|England national team]]; [[fashion design]]; and [[skateboarding]].<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.fiaformula2.com/Latest/zlgAh4UUPur1brvZIirMD/a-love-for-family-motogp-and-maths-behind-the-visor-with-arvid-lindblad |title=A love for family, MotoGP, and maths: Behind the Visor with Arvid Lindblad |date=14 August 2025 |website=[[FIA Formula 2 Championship]] |publisher=[[Formula Motorsport Limited]] |access-date=8 March 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20251010184740/https://www.fiaformula2.com/Latest/zlgAh4UUPur1brvZIirMD/a-love-for-family-motogp-and-maths-behind-the-visor-with-arvid-lindblad |archive-date=10 October 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref><ref name="GQ2026"/> Since 2024, Lindblad has lived with his parents near [[Lisbon]], Portugal.<ref>{{Cite magazine |url=https://www.autohebdo.fr/actualites/monoplace/formule-2/arvid-lindblad-fan-inconditionnel-de-motogp-et-de-marc-marquez.html |title=Arvid Lindblad, fan inconditionnel de MotoGP et de Marc Márquez |trans-title=Arvid Lindblad, unconditional fan of MotoGP and Marc Márquez |last=Glo |first=Valentin |date=15 August 2025 |magazine=Auto Hebdo |language=fr |issn=0395-4366 |access-date=8 March 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260308035412/https://www.autohebdo.fr/actualites/monoplace/formule-2/arvid-lindblad-fan-inconditionnel-de-motogp-et-de-marc-marquez.html |archive-date=8 March 2026 |url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |url=https://feederseries.net/2025/12/02/the-path-lindblad-took-to-earn-his-2026-racing-bulls-f1-seat/ |title=The path Lindblad took to earn his 2026 Racing Bulls F1 seat |last1=Lloyd |first1=Martin |last2=Kra-Caskey |first2=Calla |last3=McClure |first3=Michael |date=2 December 2025 |website=Feeder Series |access-date=8 March 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260101153413/https://feederseries.net/2025/12/02/the-path-lindblad-took-to-earn-his-2026-racing-bulls-f1-seat/ |archive-date=1 January 2026 |url-status=live}}</ref> He holds both British and Swedish citizenship.<ref>{{cite web |last1=Edmondson |first1=Laurence |last2=Saunders |first2=Nate |title=F1 predicted running order for 2026: Who is on top of the new cars? |url=https://www.espn.co.uk/racing/f1/story/_/id/47988020/f1-predicted-running-order-2026-top-new-cars |website=ESPN |access-date=17 June 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260308004435/https://www.espn.co.uk/racing/f1/story/_/id/47988020/f1-predicted-running-order-2026-top-new-cars |quote=The 18-year-old, who holds dual British and Swedish citizenship, has had a studious approach to his first F1 preseason ahead of a year many have predicted will overwhelm the sport's youngest competitors given the new cars' technical complexity.|date=21 February 2026|archive-date=8 March 2026}}</ref>

In an interview with ''[[Test Match Special]]'' on 16 July 2026, Lindblad revealed that he did not have his driving licence yet, but is working towards it.<ref>{{cite podcast |host= Elly Oldroyd|date=2026-07-16 |title=Test Match Special, Root's 99 not out helps England beat India to level ODI series |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/sounds/play/p0nzcjk6?partner=uk.co.bbc&origin=share-mobile |work= |publisher= BBC|time=30:00 |access-date=2026-07-19}}</ref>.

